# I04.var10 prospective hour-11 transit contract

**Status: contract design only.** No I04.var10 package, run directory, input, runner, SSH preflight, or native execution has been authorized. The accepted I04.var03 v1.0.1 parent is read only and is not rerun.

The proposed input changes six cells: `ProblemDescription.PDESC`; `Control.SIMPE` and `Control.RCEND` from 36 to 11; both `ResultCollection.RCEND` values from 36 to 11; and the single `SystemTransfer.TFDT` from 0.5 to 2. It also deletes the complete scheduled hour-20 `OperationProfile` row while retaining the hour-8 row. This seventh source difference is explicit support for the shorter horizon: an accepted E02 hour-11 contract review recorded converter error #204 when later scheduled profile rows remained. Authored topology is predicted as 34 tables, 21 populated rows, 211 cells; native export is predicted as 34 tables, 39 rows, 395 cells, including 18 all-null placeholders.

The accepted original shows numeric aircraft ID 0 ready after its first mission and physically departing `TEACH-UNIT` at 10.5. A 2-hour BETWEEN delay gives a calculated arrival at 12.5, beyond the hour-11 stop. The strict log oracle changes only the original numeric horizon header `36` to `11` and requires the original lines 3–61 in the same order: 61 physical lines, 53 timed records, ending in the 10.5 transfer-out. It rejects any arrival, second mission, altered identity, extra horizon diagnostic, missing line, or reordered line. The calculated 12.5 arrival is not an observed event.

The strict report oracle has four tables and 1,244 cells: one description row, one 11-column summary row, and 22 half-hour SystemResults plus 22 StockTotalResults rows for `[0,11)`. Every row value is generated from the declared mission and physical ledger. Both IDs are assigned over h7–10, fly h8–10, and are reserved h7–8; ID 0 is in transit over h10.5–11. This gives system-hour integrals NSYRY 15.5, NSYMA 6, NSYMO 4, NSYMR 2, and NSYA 21.5. The last bin predicts NSYRY and NSYA of 1. The earlier accepted parent rows only corroborate the independently generated first 22 bins. Summary values and every zero/null field are **prospective terminal-presentation predictions**. The separate accepted E02 hour-11 case shows that terminal accounting can alter preceding bins, so a different I04 field or null value is a NO_GO, not a value to fit after observation.

The short proposed physical native directory is `tmp/native-runs/i04v10-v100-20261008-01`, currently absent. Its diagnostic `File:` line must be the forward-slash absolute path to `model.sxi`, 121 ASCII bytes and below the 199-byte preflight bound. Any eventual manifest, actual SSH preflight, independent approval, invocation, and closure must bind the same absolute native directory and recheck absence and ancestor attributes. Converter zero errors, exactly warnings 108 and 126, zero notes, exact Input/Output/File paths, original streams, and actual integer exits remain required. The source is bound to distinct current catalog 499 local CRLF and Git LF byte identities; typed equality does not imply byte equality.

This hypothesis is limited to one pinned source, seed, engine, and hour-11 horizon. It proves no later arrival, general transfer rule, GUI behavior, cross-engine result, or performance. All predicted log and report values must be fixed before a native call. Any mismatch preserves the original failure and requires a newly reviewed contract rather than widening this one. The first unexecuted retained-profile draft, a decoded-only generator syntax failure, the wrong-manual-pin/header draft, and the unexecuted copied-report/wrong-File-line draft remain separately pinned in `contract.json`.
